+## Explanation of the changes
+
+1. **`src/_pytest/mark/evaluate.py`** — `cached_eval` cached the compiled/evaluated condition expression keyed only by the expression string, stored on the `Config` store. Since evaluation depends on the item's globals (from the test module), two modules with the same condition string but different globals collided, producing incorrect results. I removed `cached_eval` (plus its now-unused `StoreKey`/`evalcache_key` and the `Any`/`Config` imports) and inlined the `compile`/`eval` directly into `MarkEvaluator._istrue`, so evaluation is always performed with the current item's globals.
+
+2. **`testing/test_skipping.py`** — Added a regression test where two modules share the same `skipif("skip")` condition but define `skip = True` / `skip = False`; the test is skipped in one module and fails in the other.
