+## What changed
+
+- `src/_pytest/mark/evaluate.py`: removed the module-level `cached_eval` helper (and its `evalcache_key` `StoreKey` plus the now-unused `Any` and `Config` imports), and inlined the `_pytest._code.compile(...)` / `eval(...)` call directly in `MarkEvaluator._istrue`, so the condition is always evaluated against the current item's globals instead of a shared cache keyed only by the expression string.
+- `testing/test_skipping.py`: added `test_skipif_mark_uses_test_module_globals`, which reproduces the bug with two modules that share the same `skipif("skip")` string but define `skip = True` / `skip = False`.
